  Next question: [1mwhat actually goes in it.[0m Right now the app has no settings at all — just a username field, a password
  field, and a submit button. So the preferences subsystem needs at least one real preference to store, or there's
  nothing to persist and nothing to test against.

  One thing I'll rule out up front regardless of your answer: the password never gets stored. [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m is readable
  by any script on the origin and persists indefinitely — a remembered password there is a credential leak, not a
  convenience feature. "Remember me" will mean remembering the username only.

